# SECTION 3 - RESTLESS HOUR   b43-65   (2:47 - 4:12)
# Più mosso (T=72).  The harmony darkens: a chromatic descending bass, G minor,
# the Neapolitan C major (the cello's highest note, C6, ff), diminished
# chords.  The cello is urgent: triplets, octave and sixth leaps.  Then the
# Song's opening is heard in the shadows (G minor, low) under a high measured
# tremolo, and a cadenza over the F# pedal.  The Dusk voice returns (b63).

# -- b43-48: chromatic bass B-A#-A-G#-G-F#; the cello in triplet waves, then
# -- octave and sixth leaps.  The heartbeat doubles (lub-dub) and the violas pulse
# -- off the beat.
# -- b49-54: Em - C#halfdim7 - C/E (the Neapolitan: the cello's highest note, C6)
# -- - A#dim/E - Bm/F# - F#7: the Song's half-cadence figure, now ff.
== b43-54 [Restless Hour] ==
@ T=72 M=4/4 K=bm "Poco più mosso, inquieto"
@@ b43 T=72
@@ b51 T=76 "spingendo"
@@ b53 T=72
@@ b54 T=66 "allargando"
vcs:   | {ks:Legato Slur} 8t {mf}{"agitato"} [f#3 b3 d4 4 f#4 8t e4 d4 c#4 4 d4] | 8t [c#3 f#3 a#3 4 c#4 8t f#4 e4 c#4 4 a#3] | 8t {<} [a2 d3 f#3 4 a3 8t d4 f#4 b4 4 a4] | 4. [d5 8 b4 4 g#4 8 f#4 g#4] | 8 {f} g3> [g4 4 bb4 8 a4 g4 4 d5] | 4. {>} [e5 8 c#5 4 a#4 f#4] | 8 {mf} e3> [b3 4 g4 8 f#4 e4 4 b4] | 8 [c#4 e4 4 g4 8 f#4 e4 4 c#5] | 4. {f}{<} [e5 8 g5 4 c6> 8 b5 g5 | 4. g5 8 e5 4 c#5 8 a#4 c#5 | 4. {ff} f#5 8 e5 4 d5 8 c#5 d5 | 4 {>} e5 8 d5 c#5 2 a#4] |
